{{plinkp|Body tiara}} [[Talisman]] imbued [[tiaras]] require 1 [[Runecraft]] to make, they range from [[air tiara]]s to [[body tiara]]s and each yield 5 times the amount of experience from runecrafting their respective rune. Making one requires a [[tiara]] and a corresponding talisman to use on the respective altar. This method yields the fastest free-to-play Runecraft experience rates, except for stacked up [[runecrafting cores]]. 

Optimal experience rates of up to 47,000 experience per hour can be attained by using a dangerous [[PvP World]], teleporting to [[Barbarian Village]] using a skull sceptre (i), running to the [[Body Altar]], and making the body tiaras. [[Lumbridge Teleport]] for the closest [[bank]] and repeat. This requires 31 [[Magic]], a [[staff of air]], [[law rune]]s, and [[earth rune]]s, as well as enough [[bone fragments]] to recharge the [[skull sceptre (i)]]. [[Energy potion]]s will be necessary to keep your run [[energy]] up. It may be more efficient to carry [[air rune]]s instead of using a staff of air in order to lower your weight by 2.5&nbsp;kg at the added cost of spending air runes to teleport.

If avoiding [[PvP World]]s, the closest teleport to a bank is the [[Falador Teleport]]. 

